A hitbox knows the dispatch node of the element that inserted it, so a hit test can tell an element's ancestors.

What: A hitbox records its element's dispatch node (`Hitbox::dispatch_node`, remapped when a cached view's prepaint
is reused). `insert_hitbox` sets it from the active dispatch node; `reuse_prepaint` copies the cached hitboxes after
the dispatch subtree is reused and maps each node to its new id.

Why: 0049's occlusion (`HitboxBehavior::BlockMouseExceptAncestors`) keeps hit only the hitboxes on a native view's
dispatch path, which needs each hitbox's node. `Hitbox` is GPUI's own type, so this is a core patch (rule 12).
Nothing reads the field outside this patch until 0049.

Test: none of its own; 0051's `native_view::tests::window_input` rows hit-test through it, and the existing
cached-view tests keep passing.

Upstream PR: not filed (filing paused, patch rule 14).

